    "case_id": "473",
    "case_summary": "A 3-month-old female patient, previously healthy full-term baby without any complications during pregnancy or delivery. Exclusively breastfed with up-to-date immunizations. Initial symptoms started Feb 2-5 with rhinorrhea and nasal congestion, without cough, vomiting, diarrhea, wheezing, or dyspnea. Patient appeared fussy but breastfed normally. On Feb 6, developed low-grade fever (axillary temperature 37.6°C). History of close contact with grandmother who had rhinorrhea and throat irritation.\n\nPatient appeared well with:- Body weight: 6.5 kg- Axillary temperature: 36.5°C- Respiratory rate: 45 breaths per minute- No dyspnea, wheezing, or chest retraction- Oxygen saturation: 98% on room air- Normal breath sounds without rhonchi or crepitations- Heart rate: 140 beats per minute without murmur- Other physical exams: unremarkable\n\nLaboratory Tests:- White blood cell count: 10.23 × 10⁹ cells per L- Absolute neutrophil count: 1.19 × 10⁹ per L- Lymphocyte count: 8.3 × 10⁹ cells per L- Platelet count: 230 × 10⁹ cells per L- Hemoglobin: 112 g/L- C-reactive protein: 0.32 mg/L- Procalcitonin: 0.08 ng/mL- Creatine kinase: 224 U/L- Lactate dehydrogenase: 327 U/L- Aspartate aminotransferase: 59.9 U/L- Alanine aminotransferase: 34.8 U/L- Serum creatinine: 36.5 μmol/L- Immunodeficiency screening: unremarkable- Influenza and respiratory panel: negative- RT-PCR tests from nasopharyngeal swabs: positive (Feb 8)Imaging Studies:- Chest radiograph  Image Title: Chest X-ray  Image Description: Normal except for mild enlargement of the mediastinum shadow- Cardiac ultrasound: no abnormalities",
